WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.190
Open AI Assistant and describe one incident in plain language.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:09.300
Include the studio, the exact equipment, what happened, and what kept the class running.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.270
In this report, mic four loses audio when the instructor turns.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.430
Send the report and wait for the assistant's intake card.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.920
Treat the classification as a suggestion.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:24.560
The text says microphone, but the suggested category is not the repair route this incident needs.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.350
Choose Repair and Maintenance, then Audio, Mic and Headphone Malfunction.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.770
Check the selected studio against the report.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:38.000
Identify the area as Barre Studio, the device as Headset mic, and the problem as Cutting out.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.450
Answer the remaining questions from the incident, not from a guess.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:48.060
The next class, when it started, whether the unit is in use, and the impact on the member experience are different facts.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.610
Select Review ticket.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.020
This is still a draft.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:55.860
Read its title, routing and issue details; correct a mismatch before approval.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.960
Select Approve and create once.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.920
Wait for the created ticket number before opening the record.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:06.050
Compare the ticket header with the draft, then reload and confirm the same number persists.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.750
A completed chat exchange by itself is not proof of a saved ticket.
